  "generated_text": "To find the number of triangles that can be formed using the vertices of a regular dodecagon, we need to choose 3 vertices out of the 12 available vertices. This can be done using combinations.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 vertices out of 12 is given by the combination formula:\n\\[ \\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12!}{3!(12-3)!} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 220 \\]\n\nTherefore, there are $\\boxed{220}$ triangles that can be formed using the vertices of a regular dodecagon.",
